tiff,\n                                   9\n                                                                                              INTERIM ORDER RE SEPTEMBER 2,\n                                                 v.                                           2026 DISCOVERY DISPUTE\n                                  10\n\n                                  11     CHEN SHI, et al.,                                    Re: Dkt. No. 410\n                                                        Defendants.\n                                  12\nNorthern District of California\n United States District Court\n\n\n\n\n                                  13\n\n                                  14          On September 8, 2026, the Court held a hearing on the parties\u2019 September 6, 2026\n\n                                  15   discovery dispute. Dkt. No. 410. As discussed at the hearing, the Court requires additional\n\n                                  16   information before it can resolve this dispute.\n\n                                  17          1. Apple shall promptly provide to defendants a list of the specific documents (or\n\n                                  18              categories of documents) it requests from defendants, as well as a list of the specific\n\n                                  19              questions it wishes defendants to answer. To the extent Apple contends the documents\n\n                                  20              and information it seeks are within the scope of existing document requests or\n\n                                  21              interrogatories, it shall include a reference to the corresponding discovery request for\n\n                                  22              each item on the list.\n\n                                  23          2. Thereafter, the parties shall confer about the nature and scope of documents and\n\n                                  24              information requested in an effort to reach agreement on what, if anything, defendants\n\n                                  25              (or a subset of defendants) will produce.\n\n                                  26          3. By September 14, 2026, the parties shall jointly file Apple\u2019s list of documents\n\n                                  27              requested and questions to be answered, together with defendants\u2019 brief statement for\n\n                                  28              each item on the list indicating whether a defendant agrees to produce the documents\n\f                                        Case 5:25-cv-07105-EKL         Document 421         Filed 09/08/26      Page 2 of 2\n\n\n\n\n                                   1             requested or answer the questions posed, and if not, the principal objection on which\n\n                                   2             that defendant relies (e.g., relevance, interference with foreign criminal investigation).\n\n                                   3             No party shall include argument in the joint submission.\n\n                                   4         IT IS SO ORDERED.\n\n                                   5   Dated: September 8, 2026\n\n                                   6\n\n                                   7\n                                                                                                   Virginia K. DeMarchi\n                                   8                                                               United States Magistrate Judge\n                                   9\n\n                                  10\n\n                                  11\n\n                                  12\nNorthern District of California\n United States District Court\n\n\n\n\n                                  13\n\n                                  14\n\n                                  15\n\n                                  16\n\n                                  17\n\n                  